WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:08.508
♪♪

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:11.094
Neil Cross:
I think about every episode as
being a different 

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:12.554
chapter in a travel narrative.

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:13.847
♪♪

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:14.681
So what do I do?

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:15.974
Go left.
Right here.

00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:16.975
Allie:
HERE!

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:19.102
(Tires squealing)

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:21.521
Rupert Wyatt:
The book itself is, is very
patriarchal

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.900
because the main character is
not the most empathetic of
individuals and

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.527
Rupert Wyatt:
he's somebody who wants to sort
of rip his family away

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:30.489
Rupert Wyatt:
from the clutches of the 20th
century and all of it's commercialism

00:00:30.489 --> 00:00:32.866
and materialism and take them to
a new Eden.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.160
We're gonna chase the weather
out in Mexico.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.161
To where?

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:39.414
Mexico. Sip some tequila. Go
swimming. Go fishing. 

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.208
You don't eat enough fish, you
need to eat more fish.

00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:42.834
We don't even know anyone there.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:47.506
The tv show employs this couple,
this family of four, not making
a choice to leave

00:00:47.506 --> 00:00:48.507
Rupert Wyatt:
but they're on the run.

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:49.883
(Door shatters)

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.928
Justin Theroux:
Neil Cross is the shepherd and
guardian for the scripts,

00:00:52.928 --> 00:00:57.182
he came up with a really good
device of basically knowing that
there needed to be

00:00:57.182 --> 00:01:01.061
Justin Theroux:
something at the backs of the
foxes, meaning this government

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:03.814
Justin Theroux:
agency that is sort of chasing
them out of the United States.

00:01:03.814 --> 00:01:05.440
♪♪
Police:
Spread out!

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.441
Let's go.

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:08.694
♪♪

00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:10.946
Rupert Wyatt:
Visually what we tried to do was
to show that 

00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:13.824
two very different worlds. One
that was very clean and
fluorescent,

00:01:13.824 --> 00:01:16.743
Rupert Wyatt:
and then an outside world, in
the case of where they're headed

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:20.080
Rupert Wyatt:
that was much more unordered,
unpredictable.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.292
Rupert Wyatt:
The colors more of a kind of
blend of different influences

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:24.293
Rupert Wyatt:
and sources.

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:26.712
♪♪

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:29.881
We're, more often than not,
quick to judge what a migrant is

00:01:29.881 --> 00:01:33.176
Rupert Wyatt:
and in this instance it's a
white, nuclear, American family

00:01:33.176 --> 00:01:35.178
Rupert Wyatt:
going into a wholly different
culture.

00:01:35.178 --> 00:01:36.179
♪♪

00:01:36.179 --> 00:01:39.933
We take them from "this is their
environment, this is their life"

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.643
and we take it all away from
them.

00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:42.644
We gotta go!

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:57.117
♪♪

